# Cursor Editor — VS Code Extension Architecture

## Overview

Cursor is built on VS Code and extends it with **18 custom extensions** (published by `anysphere`) that transform it from a standard code editor into a full agentic coding platform. These extensions add 8 architectural layers on top of VS Code's ~130 bundled extensions.

```
Cursor Extension Architecture (v3.7.21)

Cursor/resources/app/extensions/
├── cursor-agent-exec           # Layer 1: Agent executor (9 MB, native deps)
├── cursor-agent-worker         # Layer 1: Agent launcher (2 MB)
├── cursor-always-local         # Layer 6: Local experiments + SCM
├── cursor-browser-automation   # Layer 4: Browser MCP server
├── cursor-checkout             # Layer 5: Git branch checkout
├── cursor-commits              # Layer 5: Commit tracking (dep: vscode.git)
├── cursor-deeplink             # Layer 2: URI deep-link handler
